A table and one of its columns renamed together: two steps, the column's
named in the table's new name, since it runs after.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch'), (2, 'dinner');

== after
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE menu RENAME TO meal;
ALTER TABLE meal RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 2
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE menu RENAME TO meal;
  step 2
    ALTER TABLE meal RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `meal`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "meal" RENAME TO "roux_old_meal"
  table `meal`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `meal`: its rows, by id, name
    INSERT INTO "meal" ("id", "name") SELECT "id", "name" FROM "roux_old_meal"
  table `meal`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_meal"

== query
SELECT id, name FROM meal ORDER BY id

== rows
1 | lunch
2 | dinner
